  "confirmed_mechanisms": [
    "All role_guidance is projected unconditionally, including when semantic selection returns no skills.",
    "SemanticPlanner reads keyword-selected full skill views before producing the semantic selection. Rejecting a skill downstream cannot remove prior conditioning.",
    "The original faulty financial plan mapped the June endpoint to serial 42159, which is June 4. QueryBuilder reused it; successful SQL did not imply valid task scope.",
    "Full-memory and no-memory verifier probes each accepted that same wrong plan in all three replicates. Removing memory alone did not repair it.",
    "In the housing case, two of three no-memory planner probes still requested only the largest plot ratio; this omission is not uniquely caused by memory.",
    "The original baseline cost-dimensions answer scored full once but 0.75 in all three blind rejudges; its originally reported regression is not robust to judge variation."
  ],
  "hypotheses_not_proven": [
    "Unconditional/global and broad index instructions may bias requirement decomposition; whole-dialog ablation still needed.",
    "Shared upstream assertions can anchor verification; hiding the plan alone also produced an incorrect calendar interpretation and an empty response.",
    "Added instruction length increased cost, but no output truncations or parse failures occurred in the completed four-arm search; token exhaustion is not demonstrated as the cause."
  ],
